This rule will detect potential command injection vulnerabilities in the Taskwarrior server. The vulnerable function or method is `mark_task_done`, which uses `execSync` without proper sanitization of input data. It's a good practice to avoid using exec functions when possible, as they can lead to code injection attacks. Instead, consider using libraries that provide safe execution of commands or parameterize your command strings. For example:
```javascript
const { execFileSync } = require('child_process');
let task_args = ['limit:'];  
if (parsed.data.tags) {  
  for(let tag of parsed.data.tags) {  
    task_args.push(`+${tag}`);  
  }  
}  
if (parsed.data.project) {  
  task_args.push(`project:${parsed.data.project}`);  
}  
task_args.push('next');  
const content = execFileSync('task', task_args, {   
  encoding: 'utf8',  
  maxBuffer: 1024 * 1024 * 10   
}).trim();
```

